= The Retirement of DuFour

Having left office, DuFour has retired from public life, withdrawing to care for his family.

The nation pays tribute to its elder statesman and former president. Even for committed <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">icans</span>, this is a bittersweet moment. Even though he was a manifestation of Heartland militarism and monarchism, he still led the nation through difficult times, without destroying democracy. It could always have been worse.

With DuFour's departure from public life, it seems as if an era of history is closing. The worst years of crisis are over, and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Imperial Sovereigntism</span>'s days are numbered. Perhaps the Commonwealth will finally enter into a new era of genuine peace...

- @game_over_1934: Bring the era to a close.
- @root: Play on.